From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 07:32:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] library: keep panorama cell shapes stable while scrolling

Panorama cells were laid out with a default wide shape and resized when each
cover decoded, so a staggered grid remeasured every lane on every image. The
shape switch also called MangaCover.Panorama and MangaCover.Book at two sites,
which disposed AsyncImage and decoded the cover again. Those height changes
while scrolling are what twitched the fast scroller.

Shapes are now remembered across process restarts and prefetched from cached
cover files, applied to a cell only once the grid is still (unless the new
ratio keeps the same wide/tall cell), and drawn through a single AsyncImage
call.

Harmony-only: same change as mihon-harmony 0018; Animeko has no such grid.
